"mrt.help.button" = "How the tool works";
"mrt.help.title" = "How it works";
"mrt.help.intro" = "First select the files, then open the tool. It renames all the selected files at once by the rules you set. The preview below shows old name → new name; nothing changes until you press Rename.";
"mrt.help.masks.title" = "Name and extension mask";
"mrt.help.masks.body" = "What the new name is built from. Plain text is kept as-is; placeholders in square brackets are replaced for each file.\n• [N] — original name without extension, [E] — extension.\n• Part of the name: [N1-5] — characters 1 to 5, [N3] — just the 3rd.\n• The Tags button inserts every available placeholder.\nExample: mask «Trip_[N]» turns «IMG_1.jpg» into «Trip_IMG_1.jpg».";
"mrt.help.counter.title" = "Counter [C]";
"mrt.help.counter.body" = "Automatic numbering — put [C] in the mask.\n• Start — the first number.\n• Step — how much to add each time (1 → 1, 2, 3; step 2 → 1, 3, 5).\n• Digits — the width, zero-padded (2 → 01, 02) so files sort correctly.\nExample: mask «photo_[C]», start 1, step 1, digits 2 → «photo_01.jpg», «photo_02.jpg», «photo_03.jpg».";
"mrt.help.date.title" = "Date and time";
"mrt.help.date.body" = "Taken from the file's modification date.\n• [Y] — year, [M] — month, [D] — day, [h][m][s] — hours, minutes, seconds.\n• [YMD] — the whole date at once.\nExample: mask «[YMD]_[N]» → «20250612_report.pdf».";
"mrt.help.search.title" = "Search and replace";
"mrt.help.search.body" = "Replaces part of the name. «Search for» is what to find, «Replace with» is what to put. The four switches below refine it — described in detail under «Search switches».
Example: find «IMG», replace with «Photo» → «IMG_1.jpg» becomes «Photo_1.jpg».";
"mrt.help.switches.title" = "Search switches — what each one does";
"mrt.help.switches.body" = "«Regular expressions» — off: exact text search. on: «Search for» is a pattern (\\d+ = any digits), and matched groups (…) go into «Replace with» as $1, $2.\nExample: find (\\d+)-(\\d+), replace $2-$1 → «12-34.jpg» becomes «34-12.jpg».\n\n«Match case» — off: «abc» also finds «ABC». on: exact case only.\nExample: find «img». Off → «IMG.jpg» is replaced. On → «IMG.jpg» is left alone.\n\n«First only» — off: all occurrences are replaced. on: only the first.\nExample: find «_», replace «-». Off → «a_b_c» becomes «a-b-c». On → «a-b_c».\n\n«In extension» — off: replace in the name only. on: the extension too.\nExample: find «n», replace «N». Off → «main.png» becomes «maiN.png». On → «maiN.pNg».";
"mrt.help.case.title" = "Case";
"mrt.help.case.body" = "Changes the case of the finished name (at the very end).\n• Unchanged — leave it.\n• all lowercase → «report».\n• ALL UPPERCASE → «REPORT».\n• First letter uppercase → «Report».\n• Each Word → «My Report».\nExample: «my file.txt» + «Each Word» → «My File.txt».";
"mrt.help.subfolder.title" = "Sort into folders";
"mrt.help.subfolder.body" = "A / in the mask sorts files into folders: everything before the / is a path, and folders are created automatically.\nExample: mask «[Y]/[N]» sorts files into per-year folders — «2024/report.pdf», «2025/letter.pdf».";
"mrt.help.preview.title" = "Preview and editing";
"mrt.help.preview.body" = "The bottom shows what you'll get before anything is renamed. Problems are shown in red: two files getting the same name, or an illegal name — those rows won't rename until you fix them.\n• Double-click a new name to set it by hand for one row.\n• «Undo» reverts the last rename.\n• «Presets» save a set of settings to reuse later.";
